      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — See inline comments for details.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** `fp_command_template_v0` properly blocks legacy v0 template uploads with `EC_HOST_CMD_ACCESS_DENIED` when `fingerprint_auth_enabled()` is true. However, in `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_template.cc`, `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` sets `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` without clearing it, and the added `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` call in `fpsensor_before` does not clear `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` (because `fp_reset_context()` intentionally preserves that bit), leaking the session state into subsequent tests.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Enforcing `fingerprint_auth_enabled()` in `fp_command_template_v0` fits cleanly with the existing fingerprint auth command guards. Moving the guard clause to the very start of `fp_command_template_v0` avoids unpacking unused request fields on rejected calls.\n* **Code Simplicity:** In `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_template.cc`, `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` in `fpsensor_before` is redundant with the `FP_CONTEXT_ASYNC` reset immediately below it, and `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` can declare `struct ec_params_fp_template` directly instead of allocating and casting a raw byte buffer.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Avoid the C-style cast `(struct ec_params_fp_template *)params_buffer` and magic size literal `8` in `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` by value-initializing `struct ec_params_fp_template` directly, matching `test_fp_template_v0_busy` in the same file.\n* **Security:** Blocking unauthenticated v0 template modification paths when fingerprint auth is active prevents arbitrary template injection and forces template operations through the v1 path.\n* **Testing:** In `test_fp_command_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` (`fpsensor_auth_commands.cc`), zero-initializing `test_v0_template_layout` leaves `params.size \u003d\u003d 0` with `sizeof(params) \u003e offsetof(ec_params_fp_template, data)`, which would fail the input size check with `EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM` even if auth were disabled; using `ec_params_fp_template params{}` (or populating `test_v0_template_layout`) ensures the test isolates the auth check.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** `Size: M (+51, -0)`. The CL is small and focused on a single logical security change with its corresponding unit tests.\n* **Commit Message:** The commit message clearly explains the security motivation and change.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/70b3cb3a-2f47-46d5-b38c-58b2bab865b1)",
