      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Calling `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` here has two issues:\n\n1. **It does not clear `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED`:** `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` calls `fp_reset_context()` (`common/fpsensor/fpsensor_state.cc`), which intentionally preserves the session flag (`global_context.fp_encryption_status \u0026\u003d FP_ENC_STATUS_SEED_SET | FP_CONTEXT_SESSION_NONCE_SET | FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED;`). As a result, once `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` sets `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED`, that flag remains set for all subsequent tests in the `fpsensor_template` suite (existing v0 tests only pass because their names sort alphabetically before `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth`).\n2. **It is redundant with `FP_CONTEXT_ASYNC` immediately below:** Lines 1603–1610 call `ec_cmd_fp_context_v1` with `FP_CONTEXT_ASYNC`, which already triggers `FP_MODE_RESET_SENSOR` and executes `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` on the `FPSENSOR` task. Calling `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` synchronously here after `RESET_FAKE(mock_alg_init)` / `RESET_FAKE(mock_alg_exit)` also increments `mock_alg_init` and `mock_alg_exit` call counts an extra time before every test.\n\nRemove `fp_reset_and_clear_context()` here and clear `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` instead (or clear it at the end of `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth`):\n\n```cpp\n\tglobal_context.fp_encryption_status \u0026\u003d\n\t\t~FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED;\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/70b3cb3a-2f47-46d5-b38c-58b2bab865b1)",
